WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.588
Begin with the actual P E endpoint and a credential reference authorized for

00:00:04.588 --> 00:00:09.638
the necessary reads Add P C context when needed Establish persistent

00:00:09.638 --> 00:00:14.200
certificate trust in the appliance and preserve the trust mount across

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.462
container replacement The certificate must match the endpoint name or

00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:23.838
address Upgrade Advisor now offers separate Verify T L S

00:00:23.838 --> 00:00:28.862
certificate controls for P E and P C inventory collection enabled by

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:33.450
default A temporary exception is administrator-only applies to that

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:38.000
inventory collection and resets afterward The exception is audited and

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.238
remains visible in saved inventory and assessment reports Keep verification

00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:47.562
enabled for normal operation and correct the trust problem This scoped

00:00:47.562 --> 00:00:52.400
inventory exception does not change drift recovery or other workflow trust

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.350
policies Workstation connectivity alone does not establish access from the

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.195
appliance

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:02.009
Open Upgrade Advisor and collect fresh inventory from the reviewed

00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:02.684
connections.

00:01:03.084 --> 00:01:06.959
Inspect discovered versions and fields that remain unknown.

00:01:07.309 --> 00:01:12.159
Enter the intended target versions and supporting evidence, then run

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.034
the assessment.

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:17.846
Review blockers, warnings, unknowns and readiness actions.

00:01:18.259 --> 00:01:21.309
Save an immutable assessment snapshot for the change record.

00:01:21.709 --> 00:01:26.471
This read-only advisor does not run an upgrade or replace vendor compatibility

00:01:26.671 --> 00:01:27.896
and lifecycle checks.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.175
Save a desired configuration for D N S, N T P and

00:01:33.175 --> 00:01:36.100
Pulse with the correct cluster and credential reference.

00:01:36.488 --> 00:01:40.438
In Drift Detection select that file and Live Prism Element as the

00:01:40.438 --> 00:01:42.750
source, then run a manual check.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.725
Every live scheduled run collects fresh settings.

00:01:47.138 --> 00:01:49.713
Stored-snapshot comparisons are a separate mode.

00:01:50.113 --> 00:01:53.863
An unknown collection result must not be counted as a healthy match.

00:01:55.059 --> 00:01:59.709
Add or edit the Automation entry, choose the correct file, source

00:01:59.721 --> 00:02:03.546
and baseline, and review the five-field U T C cron expression.

00:02:03.946 --> 00:02:06.884
Save it enabled only after the manual check works.

00:02:07.296 --> 00:02:10.934
Inspect the next actual scheduled result and its timestamp.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:12.934
Pause schedules for maintenance.

00:02:13.321 --> 00:02:17.421
Editing or enabling an entry is not proof that a scheduled read

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:18.946
has completed successfully.

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:24.117
A certificate trust failure requires the approved issuing chain or

00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:25.767
appropriate trust configuration.

00:02:26.155 --> 00:02:30.855
An I P or subject-alternative-name mismatch requires a matching endpoint

00:02:30.929 --> 00:02:31.629
or certificate.

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:37.355
A network failure requires routing, firewall, name-resolution or target-service

00:02:37.355 --> 00:02:38.929
investigation from the appliance.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:43.242
These failures remain unknown, not drifted or matched.

00:02:43.642 --> 00:02:47.867
Do not disable verification or change the desired baseline just to

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.117
obtain a green result.

00:02:50.308 --> 00:02:55.258
Monitor and Verify links to Drift Detection inventory and upgrade

00:02:55.258 --> 00:03:00.633
readiness and Execution History and Logs Overview and Clusters now add

00:03:00.633 --> 00:03:05.683
explicit managed records and P E observations These are separate evidence

00:03:05.683 --> 00:03:10.671
sources with different scopes A P E observation becomes stale after fifteen

00:03:10.671 --> 00:03:16.041
minutes Overview Refresh reads saved records Collect P E health

00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:21.221
read-only explicitly contacts the target Review identity full

00:03:21.221 --> 00:03:25.508
expected membership and reported health then use the appropriate independent

00:03:25.508 --> 00:03:30.358
acceptance checks N K P Validation Evidence remains under Advanced

00:03:30.358 --> 00:03:34.771
Automation with a Preview badge and its retained sources A specialist

00:03:34.771 --> 00:03:39.858
evidence pack successful job or fresh P E Good result cannot

00:03:39.858 --> 00:03:42.578
independently declare a cluster ready for workloads
